s("S002","Apply M009 to the compact set C and the identity map V→V. The identity is continuous, so it gives a real uniform norm bound even when C is empty.",["M009"],[],[...gg,"t0","C"],[f("F001","There exists a real L with |x|≤L for all x∈C.",["C","V"],[{symbol:"L",type:"existential real"},{symbol:"x",type:"point of V"}])]),
s("S003","Choose L with the bound of F001 and set R=max(L,0)+1>0 and Q=[−R,R]^n. For x∈C, every coordinate satisfies |x_j|≤|x|≤L<R, so C⊂(−R,R)^n=int Q. H001 gives positive finite dimensions; Q is a compact measurable coordinate box. M010 with all lower endpoints −R and upper endpoints R gives |Q|=∏_{j=1}^n(2R)=(2R)^n<∞.",["H001","M010"],["F001"],[...gg,"t0","J","C","L","R","Q"],[f("F002","R>0, Q=[−R,R]^n is compact and measurable, C⊂int Q, |Q|=(2R)^n<∞, and all positive-order derivatives of u vanish on (V\\C)×int J.",["R","Q","C","V","n","u","J"])]),
s("S004","Fix r∈int J. Smoothness in H002 and the finite component formulas defining e,A,B_j,T_j,g_j imply continuity of these functions and of e_t and ∂_{x_j}g_j. The zero derivatives proved in S001 make all of these sections zero outside C. Their nonzero sets have closures contained in the closed compact set C, so each has compact support. Apply M003 to each section with X=V, Z=R and μ=dx: Euclidean Borel open sets are measurable, and Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets. Thus every listed section is integrable. Apply M009 on Q to each continuous scalar section to obtain a finite absolute bound on Q; together with zero values off Q, the usual absolute integral bound is that constant times |Q|. This also proves the supplied bounded-support estimate.",["H002","M003","M009"],["F002"],[...gg,"t0","J","C","L","R","Q","r"],[f("F003","For every ρ∈int J, all sections e(·,ρ), e_t(·,ρ), A(·,ρ), B_i(·,ρ), T_i(·,ρ), g_i(·,ρ), ∂_{x_i}g_i(·,ρ), for 1≤i≤n, are continuous, compactly supported in C, integrable, and have an absolute integral bounded by a finite uniform-in-space bound times |Q|.",["e","e_t","A","B","T","g","C","Q","J","n"],[{symbol:"ρ",type:"time in int J"},{symbol:"i",type:"integer with 1≤i≤n"}])]),
s("S005","Since V\\C is open and contains ∂Q, every section in F003 vanishes on a neighborhood of ∂Q. The time t0 belongs to int J, so e(·,t0) is integrable. Generalize over the arbitrary t0. The same argument supplies the complete existential common-support assertion and all bounds in N002 for each t0; in particular it proves integrability at every positive time.",[],["F002","F003"],[...gg,"t0","J","C","L","R","Q"])
