app("A004","M016","S004","Set X=V, Y=Xhat×R, μ=dx, ν=product Lebesgue, Z=R, map χ as in S002 and scalar integrand φ=H.",["All spaces and measures are their finite product Lebesgue structures and R is normed real.","F002 proves the measure-preserving property from M011 and M017.","F002 identifies χ as a measurable equivalence, hence a measurable embedding."]),
app("A005","M007","S004","Set X=Xhat, Y=R, μ and ν their product/one-dimensional Lebesgue measures, Z=R and φ=H.",["Finite products of Lebesgue measures are sigma-finite, hence s-finite; the empty product has total mass one.","F001 and F002 transport the integrable derivative section through χ to H, as stated in S004."]),
