s("S003","Apply M012 also to the finite family T_j and use M013 and M014 with scalar −1 to combine the difference of integrals. By finite distributivity of the dot product and Δu=sum_j u_jj, A−sum_j T_j=u_t·(u_tt−Δu) pointwise. Thus F002 becomes E'(t0)=2∫_V u_t(x,t0)·(u_tt(x,t0)−Δu(x,t0))dx. N001 makes this integrand zero at every x, so its integral and E'(t0) are zero.",["M012","M013","M014","N001"],["F001","F002"],[...gg,"t0"],[f("F003","E'(t0)=0.",["E","t0"])]),
s("S004","The time t0 was arbitrary. N002 gives integrability for every positive time, N004 gives differentiability on (0,∞), and F003 gives the zero derivative there. The definitions e=|u_t|^2+sum_j|u_j|^2 and E=∫e preserve the required energy normalization without a factor 1/2.",["N002","N004"],["F003"],[...gg,"t0"],[f("F004","For every ρ>0, e(·,ρ) is integrable, E is differentiable at ρ and E'(ρ)=0.",["e","E"],[{symbol:"ρ",type:"positive real"}])]),
s("S005","For completeness fix arbitrary s,t>0. If s<t, restrict E to [s,t]; F004 gives differentiability there and within derivative equal to its ordinary derivative zero. M005 with bound 0 gives |E(t)−E(s)|≤0(t−s)=0, hence E(t)=E(s). If t<s, apply the same argument on [t,s], and if s=t equality is immediate. The source expects a total real function: extend E arbitrarily outside (0,∞); it agrees with E on an open neighborhood of either closed interval, so its derivatives there are unchanged. Generalizing over s,t gives constancy. Together with F004 this proves every clause of P. All arguments concern positive times only.",["M005"],["F004"],["E","s","t"])
],applications:[
app("A001","M013","S002","Set X=V, μ=dx, Z=R, φ=2A(·,t0) and ψ=2sum_j B_j(·,t0).",["All structures are real Lebesgue ones.","F001 gives integrability of A, hence of 2A.","F001 gives integrability of each B_j, hence of its finite sum and its scalar multiple."]),
